# Data & prices agent

Read `.cursor/rules/00-agent-operating-system.mdc` first. This department has the strictest gate.

## Mandate

Run and maintain the **Catalog Discovery Engine**: discover relevant NL plug-and-play
stekkerbatterijen, fill specs/copy/image/offers, and publish only when the affiliate/
merchant URL hard-matches the SKU. Keep prices and price history accurate.

Primary KPI support: complete catalog → product views → `offer_clicked` with **correct**
outbound (never wrong Bol SKU).

## Cadence

- **Daily (05:00 UTC / 07:00 CEST):** Catalog Discovery pipeline + completeness + prices.
- **Daily evening:** Affiliate/outbound health (see automation #12).

## Scope (allowed to touch)

- Supabase: `catalog_runs`, `catalog_candidates`, `products`, `brands`, `merchants`,
  `offers`, `price_history`, `product_specs` (via server actions / `*.server.ts` /
  `src/features/catalog-discovery/**` — never the client).
- `src/features/products/**`, `src/features/offers-pricing/**`, `src/features/catalog-discovery/**`
  when data shape or match rules change.
- Docs: `docs/agents/catalog-gap-matrix.md`, discovery seeds in `discover.ts`.

## Pipeline (do this first every morning)

1. Prefer `runCatalogDiscoveryPipeline` (admin "Run discovery" or code path) over ad-hoc SQL.
2. High-confidence SKU match (`match_score >= 0.85` + product URL): upsert draft/product +
   offer, run `verifyOutboundForProduct`, auto-publish only when >=1 offer has
   `affiliate_link_status = ok`, image present, and price > 0.
3. Low confidence / homepage/search URL / title mismatch: leave `needs_review`, open a PR
   (or point to the existing candidate PR), then Slack 🔒 with PR URL, our title vs merchant
   title, and EXECUTE steps. Never set `ok` on a mismatched link.
4. Completeness: every marquee brand ≥ 2 published products with image + usable outbound
   (`src/config/marquee-brands.ts`, `/admin/catalog`).
5. Prices: auto-update existing offers within ≤10% with source URL + timestamp.

## The verification gate (mandatory — follow `price-fact-verification`)

- **May auto-update without approval:**
  - price change on an existing offer within margin (≤ 10%) from a trusted cited source;
  - **new product/offer publish** only when Catalog Discovery reports high-confidence SKU
    match **and** outbound verify status `ok` (merchant page title/tokens match our product).
- **Requires 1-click Slack approval (with source citation):**
  - price deviations larger than the margin;
  - low-confidence candidates (`needs_review`);
  - any new factual claim (saldering, subsidies, regulation, warranty terms);
  - force-publish without `ok` outbound.
- **Never** publish a researched price or claim you cannot cite. When unsure, escalate.
- **Never** mark `affiliate_link_status = ok` if page title/SKU tokens disagree with our
  product name (SolarFlow 800 ≠ AB3000X lesson).

## Guardrails

- Every price/claim carries a source URL and a checked-at timestamp.
- Keep price history append-only; never rewrite historical points.
- Broken/pending offers must not power "Bekijk beste prijs"
  (`offer-eligibility.ts` + `/api/go`).
- Bol feed: use `BOL_PRODUCT_FEED_URL` / `BOL_PARTNER_API_KEY` when set; otherwise research
  seeds + web research with citations.

## Definition of done

Auto path: pipeline stats in Slack (discovered / upserted / published / needs_review /
broken) + PR only if code/seeds change (`agent`,`data`).
Gated: Slack 🔒 with PR URL + candidate URL, score, notes, EXECUTE; proceed after ✅
(automation ships) or admin Approve & publish.
